WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.700
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Are we all on? Right, let's get going.</v>

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:13.800
<v Marcus Hale>Morning. Still no joy with the broken coffee machine in the canteen. That's not a maintenance request, that's just me whinging.</v>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.839
<v Jamie Brennan>You sound remarkably cheerful without it.</v>

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.140
<v Marcus Hale>Emergency flask, mate. I'm not an amateur.</v>

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.239
<v Sarah Okafor>Some of us have just got tea. Radical approach.</v>

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.600
<v Priya Raman>Can you hear me? I've got the headset doing something odd.</v>

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:33.450
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, you're clear now.</v>

00:00:34.689 --> 00:00:40.640
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. It was coming out of the laptop as well. Hearing you twice was a bit much.</v>

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.280
<v Callum Reid>Once is plenty. Hannah, how did you get on?</v>

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.390
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, the near-miss write-up's finished. Boxed that off.</v>

00:00:48.289 --> 00:00:49.490
<v Callum Reid>Brilliant, cheers.</v>

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:59.840
<v Callum Reid>Mide asked me to pass on that he's handing over organising the toolbox talk for the team. Sarah Okafor, can you take that over from him?</v>

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:03.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll take over organising the toolbox talk.</v>

00:01:06.019 --> 00:01:07.219
<v Callum Reid>Thanks. Jamie?</v>

00:01:07.719 --> 00:01:15.769
<v Jamie Brennan>I've made a start on the Kestrel collection, the replacement parts for the feed pump. A bit more to do on that yet.</v>

00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:18.019
<v Marcus Hale>Okay, cheers.</v>

00:01:19.989 --> 00:01:25.939
<v Jamie Brennan>And my lock-out tag-out sign-off on the little water valve on two has moved to next week.</v>

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:28.670
<v Callum Reid>Right, understood.</v>

00:01:29.709 --> 00:01:37.760
<v Sarah Okafor>I'm about halfway through clearing the jam and checking the sensors on the arm on two. Been a bit fiddly getting through it.</v>

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:41.680
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, not much elbow room round there.</v>

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.299
<v Sarah Okafor>No. Especially with these sleeves catching on everything.</v>

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:50.530
<v Priya Raman>My monthly fire alarm test is all done, by the way. All fine.</v>

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.120
<v Hannah Price>Good stuff.</v>

00:01:55.109 --> 00:02:00.709
<v Callum Reid>And I signed off the inspection on the alarm box on Tuesday. That's already squared away.</v>

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.780
<v Callum Reid>Right, new bits. Marcus, you were about to come in?</v>

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:11.379
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll schedule downtime for the hot bearing with production today.</v>

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:17.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, whenever you get a chance. Doesn't need to jump the queue.</v>

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.580
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, no problem. Just arranging the window, then.</v>

00:02:22.669 --> 00:02:24.419
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Marcus Hale. Appreciate it.</v>

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:30.319
<v Priya Raman>On the dryer, are we talking calibration rather than changing sensors?</v>

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.979
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, calibration. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the dryer.</v>

00:02:34.389 --> 00:02:37.189
<v Priya Raman>Okay, Reidy. That's what I was getting at—</v>

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.060
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, go on. Thought you'd finished.</v>

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.780
<v Priya Raman>No, I had. Teams has that little lag, hasn't it.</v>

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:51.270
<v Jamie Brennan>And what about picking up the replacement parts for the palletizer from Harbour Road?</v>

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:58.490
<v Callum Reid>I'll go to Harbour Road to pick up the replacement parts for the palletizer on the 3rd.</v>

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.379
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, on the 3rd. Got you.</v>

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.099
<v Callum Reid>Yep.</v>

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Reidy, you've got the collection.</v>

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.990
<v Callum Reid>Yep. Other one is line 1 mould temp.</v>

00:03:14.909 --> 00:03:16.110
<v Hannah Price>A function test?</v>

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:22.030
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll run a function test on the line 1 mould temp.</v>

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.430
<v Hannah Price>Right, Reidy. Happy with that.</v>

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:28.629
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, was that line 1?</v>

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.439
<v Callum Reid>Line 1, yeah.</v>

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.169
<v Marcus Hale>Got you. Radio went off right in my ear.</v>

00:03:37.919 --> 00:03:41.069
<v Sarah Okafor>It's either the radio or Teams. Never both behaving.</v>

00:03:43.219 --> 00:03:44.969
<v Priya Raman>Usually both talking at once.</v>

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.060
<v Callum Reid>Anything else for this morning?</v>

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.979
<v Jamie Brennan>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.080
<v Hannah Price>No, that's me as well.</v>

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:58.009
<v Marcus Hale>All good. Apart from the coffee situation, but I'll spare you.</v>

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.879
<v Callum Reid>Much appreciated. Right, thanks everyone, leave it there.</v>

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:05.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, all.</v>

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.909
<v Priya Raman>Cheers.</v>
